\name{cellucid_history_saved_delete}
\alias{cellucid_history_saved_delete}
\title{Delete a saved state}
\usage{
cellucid_history_saved_delete(viewer, saved)
}
\arguments{
\item{viewer}{A viewer \code{\link{cellucid_view}()} or \code{\link{cellucid_serve}()} returned.}
\item{saved}{Its id (history_saved_list). Text (at least 1 character). Required.}
}
\value{
A \code{cellucid_action_request}, at once and invisibly: the action is sent now, or when the viewer's channel opens.
\code{\link{cellucid_action_result}(request)} returns its outcome: a list of \code{dataset} (The name of its dataset), \code{name}, \code{saved}, \code{steps}.
}
\description{
Remove one saved state of this browser (an autosave or a named save, by its id from history_saved_list) with every value only it held; it cannot be brought back. The history shown stays open.
}
\details{
The viewer's action \code{history.saved.delete} (History). It acts outside the viewer's state and history (a file the person receives in the browser, a publication, or what the browser keeps for later visits), which Undo does not take back: it makes no step of the history.

When an agent (Claude, ChatGPT) runs it, the viewer asks the person first (deletes-saved); from R it is not asked.
}
\seealso{
\code{\link{cellucid_act}()} sends any action by its type, and \code{\link{cellucid_action_result}()}
collects its answer.
}
\examples{
if (interactive() && requireNamespace("SeuratObject", quietly = TRUE)) {
  data("pbmc_small", package = "SeuratObject")
  viewer <- cellucid_view(SeuratObject::UpdateSeuratObject(pbmc_small))
  request <- cellucid_history_saved_delete(viewer, saved = "state-1")
  print(request)
  # cellucid_action_result(request) waits for its outcome.
  cellucid_stop(viewer)
}
}
